# A module may be named for what it holds, and `builtin_` is an ordinary
# prefix a name may start with. The refusal that keeps a program from
# spelling `builtin_length` itself matched the head of a QUALIFIED name too,
# so importing a module whose own name began with those bytes refused every
# reference to it — `builtin_shapes/circle` read as a builtin nobody has.
pub play = print "a module may be named for what it holds"
